WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
Spring 1912.

2
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.240
One dining room in Brumley.

3
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.880
A family is celebrating an engagement.

4
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.960
Then the doorbell rings.

5
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.990
An inspector arrives, asking
about the death of a young woman.

6
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.940
A clock races through a single evening.

7
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.350
A door opens.

8
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.170
A ring is handed back.

9
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.600
Three act cards flip past.

10
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.610
And at the very end, the telephone rings.

11
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.300
Why end the play there, with a phone call,

12
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.640
not an arrest?

13
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:32.640
In this mission, you'll see how
the whole play runs in one room,

14
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:34.950
across three continuous acts.

15
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.260
You'll spot the detective
story it borrows,

16
00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.340
and how Priestley bends it.

17
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.680
And you'll track the cliffhanger
that closes each act.

18
00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.370
Your mission: explain why
Priestley ends with a phone call,

19
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.590
not an arrest.
